  "description": "Bloody Stock Market 🩸 WE DO NOT BUY DIPS",
  "body_html": "<p>A very quick update on the market:<strong> It’s red lol</strong></p><p>We have been warning about this situation since September 29th and when I sold off most of my positions on the 30th. You can <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/quick-stock-market-update?r=4z8lgl\">check out yesterday’s update</a>, and see updates on the few positions I currently hold. You can also check out my parameters for <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/2-stock-purchases-when-to-short?r=4z8lgl\">When to Short</a>. Costco and Netflix continue to consolidate in my favorite short formation. </p><p><strong>The VIX is greater than 22, and the S&amp;P 500 is no where near $6812. </strong></p><p><strong>👉 I will continue to do nothing. 👈</strong></p><p><span class=\"mention-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Thebush1414&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:12281660,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:null,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/3d221cdc-32bf-470b-96b9-928e93afc8b6_144x144.png&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;70550213-63df-4501-8df8-2be6f5e6d2ef&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"MentionToDOM\"></span> is a new investor in our group, and he is doing AMAZING! He joined literally at one of the worst times of the market, a little over a month ago…and has still managed to beat the S&amp;P 500 in one short month. If you had timed the S&amp;P 500 perfectly, perfect entries and exits, you would be up up 2.17%. If you held the S&amp;P 500 for 1 month to present, you would be down -.2%. <strong>TheBush1414 is up 4.34%, that is incredible, and beating most fund managers!</strong> He noted his lessons this month, and I asked his permission to share his comments so I could reply, noting it would likely help a lot of new people. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OwfX!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F262227d7-e670-43da-bb78-580c1639790b_484x698.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OwfX!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F262227d7-e670-43da-bb78-580c1639790b_484x698.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OwfX!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F262227d7-e670-43da-bb78-580c1639790b_484x698.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OwfX!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F262227d7-e670-43da-bb78-580c1639790b_484x698.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OwfX!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F262227d7-e670-43da-bb78-580c1639790b_484x698.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OwfX!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F262227d7-e670-43da-bb78-580c1639790b_484x698.png\" width=\"484\" height=\"698\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/262227d7-e670-43da-bb78-580c1639790b_484x698.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:698,&quot;width&quot;:484,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:116247,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/176419142?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F262227d7-e670-43da-bb78-580c1639790b_484x698.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OwfX!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F262227d7-e670-43da-bb78-580c1639790b_484x698.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OwfX!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F262227d7-e670-43da-bb78-580c1639790b_484x698.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OwfX!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F262227d7-e670-43da-bb78-580c1639790b_484x698.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OwfX!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F262227d7-e670-43da-bb78-580c1639790b_484x698.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><ol><li><p><strong>“Risk no more than 1% of portfolio”</strong></p><ol><li><p>TheBush1414 is placing small bets, for big wins. Lets assume he has a $10,000 portfolio (he could have a $billion dollar portfolio for all I know). But $10,000 is an easy number to work with. </p><ol><li><p>He sees a stock he speculates will go higher, and it trades at $150 a share now. </p></li><li><p>He does not want to risk more than 1% of his total portfolio (this is tighter than me, but I think this is great for someone starting out). </p></li><li><p>He is willing to take a -8% risk with the individual stock (this could be any number…-5%, -10%…whatever…I just chose -8%). </p></li><li><p>Max loss per share x current price</p><ol><li><p>.08 x $150 = $12 He would lose $12 a share with a stop at -8%. </p></li></ol></li><li><p>So if he only wants to risk 1% of his account, which would be $100:</p><ol><li><p>$100 ➗ $12 = 8.33 or 8 shares if he cannot do fractional shares. </p></li></ol></li></ol></li><li><p>This is a quick example of the math he is doing, and others are doing. If you ever need help figuring this out, just ask me in the <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/chat/posts/eba49e1c-42ba-410f-9f01-4540686d65aa\">Main chat</a>. Now all he has to do, is speculate correctly more often than not, and his account will gradually climb. </p></li><li><p>As he gets more comfortable with time, he can adjust his position size, or his stop ranges. This really comes down to experience, and figuring out what works best <strong>FOR YOU</strong>. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!8hkn!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fca26028d-9c1e-4664-960d-254a4104c81d_1942x914.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!8hkn!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fca26028d-9c1e-4664-960d-254a4104c81d_1942x914.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!8hkn!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fca26028d-9c1e-4664-960d-254a4104c81d_1942x914.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!8hkn!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fca26028d-9c1e-4664-960d-254a4104c81d_1942x914.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!8hkn!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fca26028d-9c1e-4664-960d-254a4104c81d_1942x914.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!8hkn!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fca26028d-9c1e-4664-960d-254a4104c81d_1942x914.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"685\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/ca26028d-9c1e-4664-960d-254a4104c81d_1942x914.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:685,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:583002,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/176419142?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fca26028d-9c1e-4664-960d-254a4104c81d_1942x914.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!8hkn!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fca26028d-9c1e-4664-960d-254a4104c81d_1942x914.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!8hkn!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fca26028d-9c1e-4664-960d-254a4104c81d_1942x914.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!8hkn!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fca26028d-9c1e-4664-960d-254a4104c81d_1942x914.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!8hkn!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fca26028d-9c1e-4664-960d-254a4104c81d_1942x914.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div></li></ol><p></p></li><li><p><strong>“Stop too tight, got stopped out often”</strong></p><ol><li><p>I trade small cap and mid cap stocks predominantly. Some people that join, think I am trading Apple or Tesla stock (barf 🤮). How you place stops on a mega cap will be very different than small caps. A -2% stop on one of my stocks…chances are you will get stopped out in the first few hours. I tend to reduce position size so that I can have a wider stop. Then, if the trade goes in my favor…I add more money to the momentum! I have an entire post on <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/losers-dollar-cost-average-down\">How to dollar cost average UP</a>. Check it out after you read this article. </p></li></ol></li><li><p><strong>“Then I tried wider stops”</strong></p><ol><li><p>Yea… it gets scarier here…entire point about starting small and building positions. Would you put a -10% stop on a $2B market cap company, the same as you would a $1T market company? Of course not…if the $1T market cap company drops -10%, it has some serious issues; whereas the $2B market cap company, that is a slow Tuesday for it. You will get used to volatility of different assets, in time. You will also figure out what you like best…some people love giant slug moving assets, like gold or <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$SPY&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span>. I do not. To help you determine your stops, you can look at the <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/90-of-traders-fail-and-100-of-them\">Free Publicly Available Tools I built</a>, and see the “Market Cap Move Estimator” tool I built. You will get a sense of how much the stock will move, based on its market cap. This will help you with your stop placements. Improve it…there is no perfect. </p></li></ol></li><li><p><strong>“Need to get better at taking profits”</strong></p><ol><li><p>I have yet to meet someone that can CONSISTENTLY, time tops. I have only done it a few times. Usually I am early (I get ragged on for this in the chat lol). Ive watch Rigetti, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$RGTI&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> skyrocket up more than 50% since I sold. Does it bother me? Not really… we sold it for a 54% gain, and it was a position we added to (DCA UP). No one can take that from me. It’s done. I could take 5 full losses (roughly), and it wouldn’t dent my portfolio. </p><ol><li><p><em><strong>When I am in a “huge” profit…I take it, especially at any sign of weakness.</strong></em> </p></li><li><p>Hindsight analysis is 100% accurate. Its always easy in hindsight. But it is completely useless. Woulda shoulda coulda. Don’t dwell on it and move on to the next great setup. </p></li></ol></li><li><p>This just takes time and experience. <em><strong>Limit your downside always</strong></em>, and squeeze as much as you can out of your winners. </p></li></ol></li><li><p><strong>“Need to get better about cutting losses”</strong></p><ol><li><p>I forget which book it was in, but I recall a line, that <strong>the most common reason why people lose in the stock market, is they hold their losers too long, and their winners not long enough. </strong></p><ol><li><p>You and me both TheBush1414. Even I am still improving on this. I should have held Rigetti longer…and cut QuantumScape, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$QS&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> far sooner (my worst trade of the year).  I am better than I was a year or two ago…I suspect over time, you and I will both get better about it. Fortunately, we are picking far more winners than losers…so its working for now. </p></li></ol></li></ol></li><li><p><strong>“I need to work on my style”</strong></p><ol><li><p>This is the part everyone has to do on their own. Have to go to work? Have a family? I do not day trade, because I have to make my daughters breakfast right around the time the market opens. Day trading doesn’t work. You have to identify the variables in your life, and fit the market into your open time. If you can’t look at charts daily…then you should be on the monthly timeframe! </p></li><li><p>Also, when it comes to style, figure out a repeatable strategy. The reason we have a high winning percentage, isn’t because I have a magic eight ball that is good. I largely play volatility contraction patterns… over and over and over and over again. Thats it. Period. I sometimes will do a croissant. This is why you hear me chanting “wait for the setup!”</p></li></ol></li><li><p><strong>“I struggle on green days”</strong></p><ol><li><p>Some of the scariest purchases we have made, were on green days. But green days…the momentum is on your side! These, in my opinion, are the best! <strong>Think about all the “buy the dip” people…who have been buying dips since October 1st: They are completely wrecked.</strong> They chose to fight the market, and go with momentum working against them. Love green days when you are buying, love red days when you are shorting. </p></li></ol></li></ol><p>That is all I have for today. We will see what the market does… if it reverses and shows some strength…or if the bloodshed will continue. It matters not. Enjoy your weekend, do not stare at charts, you wont change anything…just stress yourself out. Last but not least…Thanks for stopping by! 👍 </p><p><em>For more visit: <strong><a href=\"https://substack.com/@stocktok?utm_source=user-menu\">StockTok Main Page</a> |</strong> <strong><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/stocktok-summary?r=4z8lgl\">StockTok Positions</a> |</strong></em> <em><strong><a href=\"https://substack.com/chat/3537822\">Chat with Timothy</a> </strong></em></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p><em>Subscribers get direct access with me Monday to Friday during market hours in the chat, stock reviews and access to our StockTok Dashboard, updated daily. <strong><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe\">Subscribe Now.</a></strong></em></p><p>Other Resources: <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/\">All Publications</a><em><strong> | </strong></em><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/investing-for-beginners-10-short?r=4z8lgl\">Investing For Beginners Series</a> <em><strong>|</strong> </em><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/90-of-traders-fail-and-100-of-them?r=4z8lgl\">Tools Tim Built for TradingView</a> <em><strong>| </strong></em><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/stock-screener-frequently-asked-questions?r=4z8lgl\">Stock Screener FAQ</a> <em><strong>| </strong></em><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/losers-dollar-cost-average-down?r=4z8lgl\">How to DCA UP!</a> </p><div class=\"community-chat\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://open.substack.com/pub/tjstocks/chat?utm_source=chat_embed&quot;,&quot;subdomain&quot;:&quot;tjstocks&quot;,&quot;pub&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:3537822,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Timothy’s StockTok&quot;,&quot;author_name&quot;:&quot;StockTok 📈&quot;,&quot;author_photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r3SF!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F545d5c5a-3f40-44b0-b1a1-980901ed236d_565x565.png&quot;}}\" data-component-name=\"CommunityChatRenderPlaceholder\"></div>",
